---
// Export guide: Kicksite → BeltManager (#30). US English. Every Kicksite step is sourced to
// Kicksite's own knowledge base (kicksite.com/knowledge-base), accessed 7 Nov 2026. Kicksite
// has no article dedicated to exporting students, so the student-list steps come from its
// PIN-printing article, which uses the same Export button. No price claims here.
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BreadcrumbsEnhanced from '../../components/seo/BreadcrumbsEnhanced.astro';
import ImportSteps from '../../components/switch/ImportSteps.astro';
import Sources from '../../components/switch/Sources.astro';
import RelatedGuides from '../../components/switch/RelatedGuides.astro';

const PIN_URL = 'https://kicksite.com/knowledge-base/tip-how-do-i-print-pins-for-student-attendance-check-in/';
const PROGRAMS_URL = 'https://kicksite.com/knowledge-base/programs-section/';
const ATTENDANCE_URL = 'https://kicksite.com/knowledge-base/how-to-export-the-attendance-log-report/';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How to Export Your Students from Kicksite"
  description="Step-by-step: export your Kicksite student list and students-by-rank as CSV files, then import them into BeltManager. Sourced to Kicksite's own knowledge base, November 2026."
  type="article"
  schemaType="Article"
  publishedDate="2026-11-07"
  modifiedDate="2026-11-07"
  lang="en-US"
>
  <BreadcrumbsEnhanced
    site="beltmanager"
    items={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Switching guides', href: '/switch/' },
      { label: 'Kicksite', href: '/switch/kicksite/' },
    ]}
  />

  <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-brand-navy to-gray-900 text-white py-14">
    <div class="container-custom max-w-3xl">
      <span class="inline-block bg-brand-red/20 text-brand-red-light px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-sm mb-4">Switching guide</span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">How to export your students from Kicksite</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-300">
        Kicksite's web app has an Export button on the Students page that downloads a CSV file. Here's how to use it, how to get each student's rank, and how to bring the file into BeltManager.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mt-4">Checked against Kicksite's knowledge base on November 7, 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section bg-white">
    <div class="container-custom max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-6">Export your student list</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        Kicksite doesn't publish an article just about exporting students, but its article on printing check-in PINs [1] walks through the same export:
      </p>
      <ol class="space-y-3 text-gray-700 mb-6 list-decimal pl-6">
        <li>In Kicksite, click <strong>Profiles</strong> in the left panel, then <strong>Students</strong>.</li>
        <li>
          Check the <strong>Status</strong> filter. Kicksite says it shows only <em>Active</em> students by default, which is usually what you want: BeltManager imports students as active or trial.
        </li>
        <li>Click <strong>Export</strong>. A .csv file downloads.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-8">
        Kicksite doesn't list the file's columns. The same article refers to First Name and Last Name columns followed by many more (columns E through AI), so expect a wide file. Open it in Excel or Google Sheets, keep the columns BeltManager can use (names, date of birth, contact and guardian details) and set the rest to "Don't import" when you upload.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-6">Get each student's rank</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        If the student file doesn't include rank, Kicksite's Programs article [2] describes a second export:
      </p>
      <ol class="space-y-3 text-gray-700 mb-6 list-decimal pl-6">
        <li>Click the <strong>Programs</strong> icon in the left sidebar and choose <strong>Ranks Overview</strong>.</li>
        <li>Click <strong>Export</strong>. Kicksite says this downloads a .csv of all the students in each rank.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-8">
        Copy each student's rank into a <code>Current belt</code> column in your student file. If you teach more than one program, write it as <code>Karate: Yellow</code>, and add a <code>Group</code> column for the class each student trains in.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-6">Keep a copy of your attendance history</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        BeltManager starts counting attendance from your first class on it; it doesn't import past attendance. It's still worth keeping your history. Kicksite's attendance article [3] says: open <strong>Attendance → Attendance Log</strong>, set the date range, and click <strong>Export</strong> to download a .csv file.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700">
        <strong>Before you cancel Kicksite:</strong> check your cancellation terms with Kicksite in writing, and keep billing running there until your families are set up in BeltManager. We didn't find a Kicksite knowledge-base article about moving saved cards to another system, so ask Kicksite directly if that matters to you.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ImportSteps variant="us" from="Kicksite" />

  <Sources
    heading="Sources"
    accessed="Kicksite knowledge base pages accessed November 7, 2026"
    items={[
      { label: 'Kicksite: Tip: How Do I Print PINs for Student Attendance Check In?', url: PIN_URL, note: 'page shows "Updated September 23, 2025"' },
      { label: 'Kicksite: How to Use the Programs Section', url: PROGRAMS_URL, note: 'page shows "Updated August 29, 2024"' },
      { label: 'Kicksite: How to Export the Attendance Log Report', url: ATTENDANCE_URL, note: 'page shows "Updated August 15, 2024"' },
    ]}
  />

  <section class="bg-gray-50 py-8">
    <div class="container-custom max-w-3xl text-gray-700">
      Running a school in the US? See <a href="/us/" class="text-brand-red hover:underline">BeltManager for US martial arts schools</a>.
    </div>
  </section>

  <RelatedGuides current="/switch/kicksite/" />
</BaseLayout>
